WEBVTT

00:45.087 --> 00:47.965
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:48.257 --> 00:51.134
Private Kang Seong-jae, who is stationed
at the Ganglim Outpost

00:51.218 --> 00:53.303
has impressed soldiers and lawmakers

00:53.387 --> 00:56.348
with dishes beyond standard rations.

00:56.640 --> 00:59.059
For the soldiers at the outpost
who work so hard every day

00:59.309 --> 01:01.019
I just did my best

01:01.270 --> 01:02.896
to serve them good food

01:03.230 --> 01:04.940
so I'm thankful they enjoyed it so much.

01:05.065 --> 01:07.359
With the recent controversy
over inadequate meals

01:07.442 --> 01:10.612
We must break negative stereotypes
surrounding military food.

01:10.696 --> 01:12.864
Developing more diverse menus
seems absolutely essential.

01:13.282 --> 01:15.284
This is Jeong Min-a for Armed Forces TV.

01:19.329 --> 01:21.039
And cut. All good?

01:21.123 --> 01:23.333
- Seong-jae, what gives?
- I thought you had no girlfriend.

01:23.625 --> 01:25.252
Oh, she's not my girlfriend.

01:25.335 --> 01:27.379
Oh, I see.
So you just hug anyone like that.

01:27.713 --> 01:30.215
- No, we're really just friends.
- Hey, knock it off.

01:30.299 --> 01:33.093
Do we look like the kind of guys
who'd ask you to set us up?

01:33.468 --> 01:35.387
If that's how you think we look,
you're not wrong.

01:37.180 --> 01:38.265
Hey, Kang Seong-jae!

01:40.225 --> 01:41.226
Why haven't you been answering my calls?

01:41.476 --> 01:42.978
Well, I mean...

01:43.061 --> 01:45.647
during phone time,
I figured you'd be busy...

01:45.731 --> 01:47.566
No matter how busy I am,
I'd answer your call.

01:52.112 --> 01:53.655
- How sweet.
- Hello.

01:53.739 --> 01:56.491
-Hello.
-Hello.

01:56.575 --> 01:57.993
You must be Seong-jae's seniors, right?

01:59.161 --> 02:00.746
Please take good care of him.

02:00.829 --> 02:02.122
Of course.

02:02.205 --> 02:03.248
Don't you worry.

02:03.332 --> 02:06.793
With my dedication to this country,
I'll ensure he doesn't get a scratch.

02:06.877 --> 02:08.211
I'll be with him longer than anyone

02:08.295 --> 02:10.297
right up until he's discharged.

02:10.380 --> 02:12.299
I'll be his strongest supporter.

02:12.966 --> 02:16.178
Oh, hearing that is such a relief.

02:16.261 --> 02:17.262
Thank you.

02:17.512 --> 02:18.513
Of course.

02:19.014 --> 02:20.015
Don't mention it.

02:21.683 --> 02:22.976
All right, all right.

02:25.145 --> 02:26.146
Hello there.

02:26.855 --> 02:28.398
I'm Company Commander Hwang Seok-ho.

02:28.523 --> 02:29.941
I look forward to your article.

02:30.400 --> 02:32.569
Of course. It's about him, isn't it?

02:32.986 --> 02:36.114
I'll craft every sentence
with the care of an artisan.

02:37.115 --> 02:39.618
You seem pretty close to Seong-jae.

02:41.119 --> 02:42.788
"Close" doesn't quite do it justice.

02:44.206 --> 02:45.707
I like him a lot.

02:48.543 --> 02:49.670
Private Kang Seong-jae

02:50.337 --> 02:52.130
you're a real lady-killer, you sly dog.

02:55.509 --> 02:57.260
Hey, shouldn't you be going?
They're waiting for you.

02:57.344 --> 02:58.929
Why? I've plenty of time.

02:59.012 --> 03:00.347
Right, because you have plenty of time...

03:03.183 --> 03:05.519
Did you hear him deepening his voice
for his girlfriend?

03:05.644 --> 03:06.853
When I see him like that

03:07.187 --> 03:08.605
he's just a kid.

03:11.733 --> 03:13.193
What do you think they're talking about?

03:14.194 --> 03:15.737
Aren't you happy to see me?

03:17.072 --> 03:18.865
I'm really happy to see you here.

03:19.366 --> 03:21.535
Of course I'm happy to see you, but...

03:21.618 --> 03:23.578
It's just my situation right now.

03:24.538 --> 03:25.789
I guess being a private means

03:25.956 --> 03:27.374
you have to walk on eggshells.

03:28.417 --> 03:30.293
Still, I'm glad you seem to be doing well.

03:31.920 --> 03:33.672
I stopped by your mom's food truck.

03:33.755 --> 03:35.132
She's really worried about you.

03:35.924 --> 03:37.092
Is everything okay?

03:40.637 --> 03:41.638
Yeah.

03:57.487 --> 03:59.781
EPISODE 5

04:01.324 --> 04:02.409
WARNING
NO UNAUTHORIZED PHOTOS OR ENTRY

04:21.344 --> 04:22.345
You startled me.

04:22.846 --> 04:24.890
Go on, just break everything.
Smash it all.

04:25.182 --> 04:26.183
I'm sorry.

04:28.226 --> 04:30.812
What, you feeling restless or something?

04:33.815 --> 04:35.108
I'm getting out of here first

04:35.192 --> 04:37.611
to breathe that sweet, free air

04:37.944 --> 04:40.030
just hang in there

04:40.113 --> 04:41.823
and tell yourself you're next. Got it?

04:43.366 --> 04:44.367
Yes, I will.

04:52.918 --> 04:55.712
Communications Security.
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun, Ganglim mess.

05:07.182 --> 05:08.850
Did you forget my leave was delayed

05:08.934 --> 05:10.977
because I didn't have a replacement?

05:11.311 --> 05:12.562
I'm well aware.

05:12.646 --> 05:15.232
Then why am I the one
who has to give up my leave?

05:15.315 --> 05:18.318
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
you know about Private Kang Seong-jae.

05:18.401 --> 05:20.570
He enlisted before he had
a chance to grieve

05:20.654 --> 05:23.031
and he must be so worried
about his family.

05:23.281 --> 05:25.200
As his senior, isn't this

05:25.283 --> 05:27.494
a little tolerance you could show him?

05:27.828 --> 05:29.454
"Tol"? What?

05:32.123 --> 05:33.917
Sir, you care a lot about Seong-jae.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.336
Can't you also consider my situation?

05:36.419 --> 05:38.213
I know. Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun

05:38.296 --> 05:40.173
I know you feel slighted.

05:40.507 --> 05:42.634
But the Battalion Commander...

05:42.717 --> 05:45.136
is also very concerned
about Private Kang Seong-jae.

05:45.220 --> 05:47.180
Besides, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
you're almost discharged.

05:47.264 --> 05:48.765
I know it's tough

05:48.849 --> 05:50.225
but let's hang in there a bit longer.

05:50.475 --> 05:51.476
Come on.

05:51.893 --> 05:52.894
All right!

05:56.481 --> 05:57.482
Here.

06:05.115 --> 06:06.116
Hey, now.

06:06.199 --> 06:07.784
I used up a whole bottle of softener

06:07.868 --> 06:09.870
to do all your laundry

06:10.704 --> 06:11.705
and this is the reaction I get?

06:11.788 --> 06:12.789
It's great.

06:12.873 --> 06:15.375
When I go out,
I bet everyone will be staring at me.

06:15.458 --> 06:18.545
You trying to advertise you're a kitchen
soldier when you're on leave?

06:18.628 --> 06:20.171
We might be used to it

06:20.255 --> 06:23.008
but civilians will know right away.

06:23.133 --> 06:24.801
Yeah, what if your girlfriend goes

06:24.968 --> 06:25.969
"Ugh, what's that garbage smell?"

06:26.052 --> 06:28.722
What if she says, "You've changed.
Let's break up"?

06:29.055 --> 06:30.891
She's really not my girlfriend.

06:31.099 --> 06:33.226
Oh, yeah? Then you can set me up with her.

06:34.060 --> 06:35.228
I don't

06:35.937 --> 06:36.938
know about that.

06:37.439 --> 06:38.940
You don't know about that?

06:39.274 --> 06:41.109
No, it's not that, it's just...

06:41.318 --> 06:43.069
Min-a's not really into guys...

06:43.153 --> 06:45.447
who are super talkative.

06:49.367 --> 06:50.744
- Seong-jae.
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

06:50.827 --> 06:52.746
Getting used to military life?
Now you're dissing me.

06:53.204 --> 06:55.248
If she likes the serious
and quiet type, what about me?

06:55.332 --> 06:57.667
Hey, didn't you get dumped recently

06:57.751 --> 06:59.377
and swear off love forever?

06:59.461 --> 07:01.880
The best way to get over someone
is with someone new, man.

07:03.465 --> 07:05.550
Hey, why the long face?

07:05.634 --> 07:06.927
You're supposed to be going on leave.

07:07.844 --> 07:09.429
Well, it's just...

07:10.430 --> 07:13.808
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun
couldn't go on leave because of me.

07:14.351 --> 07:15.769
- Hey, it's fine.
- Don't worry about it.

07:32.035 --> 07:35.038
Damn, I was gonna get more body wash

07:35.121 --> 07:36.915
when I went out on leave.

07:36.998 --> 07:39.459
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun, I'm sorry.
- Kang Seong-jae.

07:40.001 --> 07:41.086
Private Kang Seong-jae.

07:46.216 --> 07:49.594
I don't want to be petty
about my junior's leave...

07:50.053 --> 07:51.554
But don't take it for granted.

07:51.680 --> 07:52.722
Yes, I'm sorry.

07:52.806 --> 07:55.767
When the Company, Battalion Commanders
are suddenly nice to you

07:56.059 --> 07:58.561
they're just looking out for themselves.

08:00.063 --> 08:02.148
So don't take it for granted.

08:04.275 --> 08:05.485
Yes, I understand.

08:18.123 --> 08:19.416
He might talk like that

08:19.499 --> 08:20.917
but he was the first one
to look out for you.

08:23.962 --> 08:24.963
Here.

08:25.046 --> 08:26.798
Oh, no, really. I couldn't.

08:26.881 --> 08:29.759
Come on, it's tradition
for your first leave. I got some too.

08:30.510 --> 08:31.553
Just take it.

08:33.179 --> 08:34.764
Everyone in our barracks

08:34.848 --> 08:36.182
chipped in a little,

08:36.266 --> 08:37.976
so go out and get something nice
to eat with your family.

08:38.685 --> 08:40.270
And don't blow it all
on your girlfriend, you hear?

08:40.687 --> 08:41.688
Gosh...

08:42.647 --> 08:43.773
Thank you so much.

08:56.369 --> 08:59.039
Reporting. Private Kang Seong-jae

08:59.289 --> 09:01.958
is granted a seven-day consolation leave

09:02.042 --> 09:03.960
effective today. Reporting.

09:04.044 --> 09:05.462
Salute!

09:06.254 --> 09:07.255
Salute!

09:08.673 --> 09:10.925
Going on your first leave.
How do you feel?

09:12.177 --> 09:13.303
I'm excited

09:13.386 --> 09:15.388
but also a little scared.

09:15.472 --> 09:17.390
Don't worry about a thing.

09:17.474 --> 09:19.017
Just go rest and have fun.

09:19.517 --> 09:21.811
But don't get so excited
that you get into trouble.

09:22.228 --> 09:23.438
Yes, I understand, Outpost Commander.

09:23.938 --> 09:25.648
- Go on, get going.
- Salute!

09:25.732 --> 09:27.525
- Go on, hurry up.
- Thank you.

09:31.321 --> 09:33.948
BAEKRIM EXPRESSWAY

09:34.032 --> 09:37.702
YOU ARE NOW LEAVING YEONJU-SI
TRAVEL SAFELY

09:39.913 --> 09:43.875
SEOUL, NAMYANGJU, GAPYEONG

09:48.171 --> 09:49.172
Hero.

09:49.506 --> 09:51.591
Check your new message.

09:58.306 --> 09:59.682
CONFIRM

10:00.016 --> 10:02.352
GARRISON AREA

10:02.435 --> 10:04.020
You have left the Garrison Area.

10:05.438 --> 10:07.315
Skill usage is restricted.

10:15.323 --> 10:18.243
TTEOKBOOKI, SUNDAE,
FISH CAKES, ASSORTED FRIED SNACKS

10:18.326 --> 10:25.375
ENJOY YOUR MEAL AND HAVE A GREAT DAY!

10:38.930 --> 10:41.516
I think the owner's been eating
too much of her own tteokbokki.

10:41.891 --> 10:43.810
You must be having
a massive blood sugar spike.

10:43.893 --> 10:45.145
Oh, welcome...

10:47.647 --> 10:48.857
What?

10:49.149 --> 10:50.275
Are you on leave?

10:50.358 --> 10:51.860
Don't you recognize your own son?

10:51.943 --> 10:53.903
Goodness, why did you come

10:53.987 --> 10:55.321
without telling me?

10:55.405 --> 10:56.990
Salute!

11:03.913 --> 11:05.248
You've been through so much.

11:09.043 --> 11:11.337
I told you to go home and get some rest.

11:11.421 --> 11:12.839
I still have plenty of time.

11:12.922 --> 11:15.300
I got extra leave as a reward.

11:17.427 --> 11:18.595
I was worried

11:18.678 --> 11:21.222
but I'm glad to see you've adjusted well.

11:27.478 --> 11:29.063
Mom, but...

11:30.481 --> 11:32.108
Isn't it a little too empty here?

11:32.942 --> 11:33.943
Well...

11:34.777 --> 11:36.988
Business is slow for everyone these days.

11:42.619 --> 11:45.330
Should I try some of my mom's
tteokbokki after all this time?

11:46.206 --> 11:47.332
- Would you?
- Yeah.

11:55.173 --> 11:56.716
You have left the Garrison Area.

11:57.175 --> 11:58.927
Skill use is restricted.

12:02.180 --> 12:03.473
- I'll give it a try.
- Okay.

12:13.024 --> 12:15.360
The sauce is just really spicy

12:16.069 --> 12:18.071
and it feels separate from the rice cakes.

12:18.738 --> 12:19.739
Why?

12:19.906 --> 12:20.907
Is it not good?

12:24.035 --> 12:25.620
Well, Dad's...

12:33.503 --> 12:35.046
It just tastes a bit different

12:35.380 --> 12:36.756
from when I had it before.

12:38.132 --> 12:41.177
No, I just copied what I saw your dad do

12:41.511 --> 12:43.054
exactly as I remembered.

12:43.763 --> 12:46.516
I guess I just don't have his magic touch.

12:46.599 --> 12:49.227
See? I told you we should've made
mala tteokbokki.

12:49.936 --> 12:53.356
Hey, I told you to help Mom out
while I was away.

12:53.606 --> 12:54.649
You think I didn't?

12:54.732 --> 12:56.859
For kids today, it's vibe over taste.

12:57.068 --> 12:58.569
You need the right aesthetic

12:58.653 --> 13:00.238
for people to post on social media.

13:01.864 --> 13:03.408
What? What aesthetic?

13:12.709 --> 13:14.502
Jeez, you actually expected
people to eat this?

13:14.919 --> 13:16.587
You were cut off from society briefly

13:16.671 --> 13:18.381
and already you're out of touch.

13:18.464 --> 13:21.676
Now people even go
to milk tea shops for tteokbokki.

13:22.051 --> 13:23.761
Plus, adding a trendy black food

13:23.845 --> 13:24.846
was the perfect combination.

13:24.929 --> 13:27.056
So did it help with business?

13:27.640 --> 13:29.183
It got us some buzz.

13:29.267 --> 13:30.560
For about a week, anyway.

13:30.643 --> 13:34.147
Of course. If it tastes bad,
they're not coming back.

13:35.273 --> 13:37.859
You probably lost
the regulars too, didn't you?

13:39.652 --> 13:41.404
Now that I'm the one doing the cooking

13:41.612 --> 13:43.072
I realize it's not easy

13:43.573 --> 13:44.866
to please everyone's palate.

13:50.121 --> 13:51.122
Should I give it a try?

13:52.999 --> 13:54.125
- What?
- You?

13:55.293 --> 13:57.378
GEUMJEONG BUSAN FISH CAKE

14:01.132 --> 14:02.842
You have left the Garrison Area.

14:03.384 --> 14:05.887
All recipes and skill use are restricted.

14:11.768 --> 14:13.853
He does know what he's doing, right?

14:14.812 --> 14:16.189
He said he was such a good cook

14:16.272 --> 14:17.857
he got a reward in the army.

14:18.733 --> 14:20.068
Let's just trust him.

14:28.868 --> 14:30.787
SEONG-JAE'S TTEOKBOKKI

14:38.586 --> 14:40.463
I was wondering when you'd ever finish.

14:40.671 --> 14:42.131
Well, you can at least
make it look the part.

14:42.423 --> 14:44.092
Look who's the food critic now.

14:44.509 --> 14:45.510
Let's eat.

14:55.686 --> 14:56.687
The thing is...

14:56.979 --> 14:59.023
I had a problem.

14:59.107 --> 15:01.776
I swear I can do much better than this.

15:02.276 --> 15:03.444
Contestant Kang Seong-jae.

15:03.986 --> 15:04.987
I'm sorry

15:05.696 --> 15:07.198
- you've been eliminated.
- Oh, dear.

15:07.281 --> 15:08.950
Ah, I really could've done a good job.

15:09.033 --> 15:10.243
I thought it was delicious.

15:11.327 --> 15:12.662
You worked hard, honey.

15:13.371 --> 15:15.081
Let's close up early today

15:15.164 --> 15:16.958
and go get something good to eat, okay?

15:19.919 --> 15:21.212
You did great.

15:21.295 --> 15:22.672
It was delicious.

15:27.301 --> 15:29.470
What's the point of good ingredients

15:30.012 --> 15:31.305
if Dong-hyun gets his hands on them?

15:31.389 --> 15:33.391
- It becomes worse than dog food.
- Hey.

15:33.599 --> 15:35.268
Once Yoon Dong-hyun is on leave

15:35.351 --> 15:36.894
Kang Seong-jae will take over.

15:37.311 --> 15:39.605
I mean, honestly,
about that reward leave he got...

15:39.689 --> 15:41.691
Didn't he get it all by riding
the New Recruit's coattails?

15:41.774 --> 15:43.484
Hey, don't say that.

15:44.569 --> 15:47.071
I'll prove that without Kang Seong-jae

15:47.447 --> 15:49.115
the mess hall runs fine.

16:09.051 --> 16:11.220
Okay! Perfect!

16:20.646 --> 16:23.232
All right. We're open!

16:23.316 --> 16:25.026
Sir! Give us all your frozen stuff.

16:25.109 --> 16:26.611
Frozen? All right, the frozen food.

16:27.778 --> 16:28.821
That way.

16:29.363 --> 16:32.992
Is the soldier who made
that delicious pork stew on leave?

16:33.075 --> 16:35.453
They're emptying the Golden Wagon.
All right, next!

16:35.536 --> 16:36.829
GANGLIM OUTPOST

16:41.209 --> 16:42.793
What is this?

16:43.878 --> 16:45.379
I knew this would happen.

16:45.463 --> 16:46.464
Yoon Dong-hyun!

16:48.090 --> 16:49.300
Yes!

16:51.093 --> 16:53.221
Hey, I told you to just
stick with what you know.

16:53.304 --> 16:56.015
Yoon Dong-hyun, what did you do
to the rice this time?

16:58.392 --> 17:00.144
So why can't I do it?

17:01.145 --> 17:02.146
What's that, you punk?

17:03.189 --> 17:04.857
I didn't leech off him.

17:05.608 --> 17:06.859
Look at you, glaring at me...

17:06.943 --> 17:08.611
I want to do a good job too!

17:12.698 --> 17:13.950
You little...

17:15.201 --> 17:17.328
What am I going to do with this kid? Jeez.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.332
My brother's on leave!

17:21.749 --> 17:22.750
YOUR BROTHER IS SO HANDSOME
IS HE IN A BAND? MY HUSBAND

17:22.833 --> 17:23.834
I DON'T NEED SCHOOL, I WANT SEONG-JAE

17:23.918 --> 17:25.044
TOP 3 MAYO DISHES: TUNA, CHICKEN,
AND SEONG-JAE, TAKE MY-O HEART

17:25.127 --> 17:26.504
SEONG-JAE, OCEAN VIEW OR CITY VIEW?
MY FAVORITE IS "I LOVE VIEW"

17:26.587 --> 17:27.838
Kang Seong-jae is on leave?

17:31.217 --> 17:32.802
Yeah, thanks.

17:34.387 --> 17:36.472
- I'll grill the meat now.
- No, it's okay.

17:37.014 --> 17:38.933
At my unit's company dinners

17:39.016 --> 17:41.435
everyone said I was the best
at grilling meat.

17:48.818 --> 17:50.611
Flipping it so much makes it tough.

17:50.861 --> 17:53.030
I was looking forward to a good meal

17:54.031 --> 17:55.575
- but this is a little disappointing.
- Come on.

17:55.658 --> 17:58.911
Hey, come on.
This pork belly is delicious.

18:00.037 --> 18:02.206
Then what did you want to eat?

18:04.166 --> 18:06.168
Some hot malatang?

18:06.544 --> 18:08.004
That darn malatang again.

18:08.087 --> 18:10.548
Kids these days bond
over malatang, you know.

18:10.840 --> 18:12.925
If I only had the money
to add fenmian noodles

18:13.009 --> 18:14.427
I could have joined in.

18:20.308 --> 18:24.437
I'll make you a pork belly wrap, okay?

18:27.773 --> 18:28.774
Here.

18:28.899 --> 18:31.277
Use this to go get malatang
with your friends.

18:33.779 --> 18:35.364
King God General Seong-jae

18:35.698 --> 18:37.283
I will do my utmost to ensure

18:37.366 --> 18:38.951
you have a pleasant leave.

18:40.870 --> 18:42.622
Where does a soldier get money like this?

18:43.873 --> 18:46.334
My superiors gave me
spending money for my leave.

18:48.336 --> 18:49.754
And this is for you, Mom.

18:50.254 --> 18:51.797
Oh, no, I can't take this.

18:51.881 --> 18:53.090
You must have so much you want to do.

18:53.174 --> 18:54.550
Why give this to me?

18:54.634 --> 18:56.218
- No, really.
- Mom, I have money.

18:56.302 --> 18:57.553
- No, really, I'm fine.
- Come on.

18:57.928 --> 18:59.347
- Honey...
- It's for you.

18:59.430 --> 19:00.514
- Oh, I really...
- Here.

19:00.598 --> 19:01.891
Just take this too, Mom.

19:02.683 --> 19:04.435
This heartwarming moment

19:04.518 --> 19:06.479
is really ruining
my appetite for malatang.

19:08.939 --> 19:10.149
Oh, you kids.

19:28.292 --> 19:29.293
Welcome.

19:29.377 --> 19:31.545
Stir-frying beef for soup.

19:31.629 --> 19:32.963
This egg is rotten.

19:33.589 --> 19:35.049
The frying temperature is optimal.

19:38.094 --> 19:40.805
You have successfully achieved
Company Dinner Satisfaction.

19:42.723 --> 19:44.058
I didn't realize it when I had it...

19:45.351 --> 19:47.353
but it's so inconvenient now
that I can't use it.

19:48.979 --> 19:51.607
But isn't it unfair I can't use it
just because I'm outside?

19:52.066 --> 19:53.067
Warrior.

19:55.361 --> 19:57.738
To use your abilities
outside the Garrison Area

19:58.197 --> 20:00.449
you must be promoted to Advanced Cook.

20:02.284 --> 20:03.869
Advanced Cook?

20:05.204 --> 20:06.789
You mean, Cook isn't the final level?

20:09.250 --> 20:12.211
BEGINNER COOK, KITCHEN ASSISTANT

20:14.922 --> 20:16.632
I still have such a long way to go.

20:19.051 --> 20:20.469
If I become an Advanced Cook

20:20.553 --> 20:23.347
I can make the food truck much bigger

20:24.181 --> 20:26.058
and we'll be able to open
a restaurant again.

20:26.308 --> 20:27.393
So when I get back

20:27.476 --> 20:30.438
I guess I have to do
quests for Experience Points?

20:31.564 --> 20:34.358
Well, there's nothing
I can do about it for now.

20:41.240 --> 20:46.954
TTEOKBOKKI RECIPE

20:51.542 --> 20:53.544
I feel like there's more to it.

21:15.399 --> 21:16.400
What is it?

21:16.484 --> 21:17.485
What's going on now?

21:17.568 --> 21:18.694
Is it a gas explosion?

21:18.778 --> 21:20.404
- What's happening?
- It's an emergency!

21:20.946 --> 21:23.449
I tried frying the rice cakes,
and it turned into a disaster, sir.

21:23.532 --> 21:25.826
You were supposed to pat them dry!

21:25.910 --> 21:27.912
Did you throw them in the oil wet?

21:27.995 --> 21:29.163
Is that really necessary, sir?

21:31.665 --> 21:33.125
Good grief.

21:33.209 --> 21:36.003
I have no idea how you
managed to cook all this time.

21:37.087 --> 21:39.340
And of all times,
Seong-jae had to be on leave.

21:39.882 --> 21:42.259
Jeez, let's just forget it.

21:42.343 --> 21:44.345
- What's this, sir?
- Hands off!

21:45.805 --> 21:46.806
This here...

21:47.181 --> 21:50.434
Congressman Kang Hong-beom said
he enjoyed his meal last time

21:50.518 --> 21:52.728
so he sent our unit these beef bones.

21:52.812 --> 21:54.647
You hear me? Don't you touch them.

21:54.980 --> 21:57.858
I'm saving them for Kang Seong-jae
to make a meal for his return.

21:58.150 --> 21:59.902
That's not fair, sir.

22:00.194 --> 22:02.112
So it's okay for Kang Seong-jae,
but not for me?

22:06.367 --> 22:08.327
Seriously? You can still say that
after the mess you just made?

22:08.452 --> 22:11.705
You don't even know what happens
when water meets oil.

22:12.540 --> 22:13.541
Goodness.

22:14.083 --> 22:16.460
Dong-hyeon. Dong-hyeon.

22:16.919 --> 22:19.672
I know you want to do well,
I get it, okay?

22:20.381 --> 22:22.424
But do not, under any circumstances,
touch these bones.

22:22.550 --> 22:23.551
Got it?

22:25.469 --> 22:26.470
Let me go.

22:26.554 --> 22:28.305
I said let go!

22:29.431 --> 22:30.891
You're seriously driving me crazy.

22:44.196 --> 22:45.322
What are you looking for so hard?

22:48.576 --> 22:49.618
Let's see... here.

22:52.371 --> 22:53.372
Found it.

22:53.455 --> 22:54.456
LOCAL CO-OP

22:55.624 --> 22:58.460
FRESH MARKET
EGGS, FISH CAKE, ROLLED SEAWEED, SQUID...

22:58.627 --> 22:59.837
Go to the market

22:59.920 --> 23:02.715
early in the morning
right when the new deliveries arrive.

23:03.132 --> 23:05.634
That's the only way to get the best
ingredients before anyone else.

23:06.719 --> 23:08.178
Why the sudden trip to the market?

23:10.014 --> 23:11.765
Oh, I've just been craving this.

23:14.351 --> 23:17.187
You two have the exact same taste, too.

23:18.564 --> 23:20.816
So, you don't come to the market
often anymore?

23:23.319 --> 23:24.612
Not as much.

23:26.030 --> 23:27.323
It's so convenient to order online

23:27.406 --> 23:29.450
and have it delivered to our door.

23:33.662 --> 23:35.623
I think it was somewhere around here.

23:37.249 --> 23:38.250
What was?

23:41.587 --> 23:42.671
-Mom, let's go.
-Where to?

23:42.963 --> 23:43.964
Why?

23:46.008 --> 23:47.384
Its chewy texture is what kept

23:47.468 --> 23:49.053
our regulars coming back for more.

23:49.303 --> 23:50.554
Even though it's a bit pricier

23:50.888 --> 23:52.348
that's why I only use rice cakes

23:52.431 --> 23:54.350
made fresh at the mill each day.

23:55.225 --> 23:56.518
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

24:00.189 --> 24:02.066
It's chewy since it's fresh, right?

24:02.441 --> 24:04.026
Yes, it's perfect. Really.

24:05.277 --> 24:06.320
But...

24:06.820 --> 24:08.155
many people prefer

24:08.238 --> 24:10.115
wheat-flour cakes for their tteokbokki.

24:10.199 --> 24:12.368
Wheat cakes get soggy easily.

24:12.451 --> 24:15.412
Fresh rice cakes feel better

24:15.496 --> 24:17.748
and they don't feel separate
from the sauce.

24:18.666 --> 24:19.833
See, Mom? Told you.

24:20.459 --> 24:21.669
Goodness.

24:24.463 --> 24:26.382
Well, well, look who it is!

24:26.465 --> 24:27.716
Oh, hello.

24:28.008 --> 24:29.969
- It's been a while.
- It really has.

24:30.052 --> 24:31.387
- Yes.
- Your son?

24:31.553 --> 24:33.138
- Yes.
- I heard he's in the army.

24:33.222 --> 24:34.723
Is he on leave?

24:35.099 --> 24:36.100
Hello.

24:36.934 --> 24:38.644
Are you Mr. Kang's family?

24:38.727 --> 24:40.020
Look at him.

24:40.104 --> 24:42.022
He's the spitting image of Mr. Kang.

24:42.106 --> 24:43.983
Oh, I take after my mom, actually.

24:44.233 --> 24:46.402
What are you talking about?
You're a carbon copy of your father.

24:46.694 --> 24:48.570
Since you're Mr. Kang's family

24:48.654 --> 24:50.114
the chili powder is on the house.

24:50.197 --> 24:52.032
- Oh, my.
- You really don't have to.

24:52.116 --> 24:54.994
Nonsense. Mr. Kang fed me a lot

24:55.077 --> 24:56.286
this is the least I can do.

24:56.370 --> 24:57.579
You choose the best ingredients

24:57.663 --> 24:59.498
with your hands, not with your eyes.

24:59.790 --> 25:01.000
Avoid any with sprouts

25:01.083 --> 25:03.335
as they've lost their sweetness.

25:03.419 --> 25:05.713
RIN'S VEGETABLE STORE
ONLY FRESH PRODUCE ARE SOLD

25:06.296 --> 25:08.841
Oh, you'll never be able to pick

25:08.924 --> 25:10.968
the good ones just by looking.

25:11.969 --> 25:13.387
See this outer skin here?

25:13.762 --> 25:16.265
It needs to be hard and stiff.
That means it's fresh.

25:16.598 --> 25:17.891
Here, hold it. See?

25:18.517 --> 25:20.477
- Yes.
- When you lift it, the heavy ones

25:20.561 --> 25:22.604
have a lot of moisture inside.

25:23.105 --> 25:25.816
And pick the ones with dry, clean roots.

25:27.109 --> 25:28.652
Wow, these onions are really good quality.

25:28.736 --> 25:29.737
Of course.

25:29.820 --> 25:32.531
Your father was so picky
about only choosing the best ones.

25:34.199 --> 25:35.743
He had a real temper

25:35.826 --> 25:37.286
if I didn't give him the good stuff.

25:38.954 --> 25:42.207
Please take good care of my mother
while I'm away.

25:42.291 --> 25:44.668
Wow, such a devoted son.

25:45.794 --> 25:46.795
Thank you.

25:46.879 --> 25:50.632
If you need sweet potatoes to fry,
just say the word.

25:50.716 --> 25:53.719
If you want,
I'll deliver them right to your door!

25:53.802 --> 25:55.846
Oh, thank you so much.

25:55.929 --> 25:57.014
Take your time looking around.

26:03.645 --> 26:06.940
OUTPOST COMMANDER
FIRST LIEUTENANT CHO YE-RIN

26:07.024 --> 26:10.152
SELECTED VENDOR
CHAESANG FROZEN FOODS, INC

26:10.235 --> 26:13.363
Nampyo Distribution...

26:14.114 --> 26:16.700
Why are you doing the inspection
instead of the Master Sergeant?

26:17.076 --> 26:21.288
NAMPYO DISTRIBUTION

26:21.371 --> 26:24.124
NO RESULTS FOR "NAMPYO DISTRIBUTION"

26:26.335 --> 26:31.381
NAMPYO DISTRIBUTION: LIVESTOCK
(PORK, BEEF), VEGETABLE, TWO YEARS

26:31.465 --> 26:34.134
The number you have dialed does not exist.

26:34.635 --> 26:35.761
This won't do.

26:36.595 --> 26:38.889
But I will be reporting this
to my superiors.

26:38.972 --> 26:41.100
Fine, do whatever you want! Damn it.

26:51.652 --> 26:52.903
IM SEUNG-BIN

27:01.036 --> 27:05.290
DIFFERENT DISTRIBUTORS...
SAME CONTACT PERSON?

27:07.126 --> 27:08.293
Yes?

27:08.710 --> 27:10.003
Outpost Commander, have you eaten?

27:10.838 --> 27:12.756
Not yet, sir. Are you heading to a meal?

27:12.840 --> 27:15.134
I feel like eating here
will just ruin my appetite.

27:15.592 --> 27:16.844
Want to try an old Chinese place?

27:16.927 --> 27:19.805
The owner has an incredible presence.

27:19.888 --> 27:22.182
Their ganjjajang is seriously
out of this world.

27:23.392 --> 27:25.561
I should probably check on the mess hall.

27:25.644 --> 27:26.812
There's something I need to look into.

27:29.690 --> 27:32.276
What is it you're looking into this time?

27:33.402 --> 27:35.112
The food vendors

27:35.195 --> 27:37.406
are ghost companies
that don't show up in searches, sir.

27:37.489 --> 27:39.491
And I can't figure out the process
by which they were selected.

27:40.784 --> 27:42.202
I just can't understand it, sir.

27:45.205 --> 27:46.415
Cho Ye-rin.

27:46.999 --> 27:49.376
That's not your duty as Outpost Commander.

27:49.459 --> 27:51.879
How many times do I have to tell you?

27:52.087 --> 27:54.089
This is all for the good of
the Outpost, sir.

27:54.173 --> 27:56.884
Forget the post, just stay out of it
for your own good.

27:57.217 --> 27:58.218
Got it?

27:58.760 --> 28:00.262
The higher-ups are gunning for you

28:00.345 --> 28:01.972
and I'm doing my best to defend you.

28:02.055 --> 28:04.266
I'm defending you,
but if you keep acting this way.

28:05.309 --> 28:07.019
You shouldn't be doing this.

28:09.605 --> 28:10.606
Company Commander.

28:11.523 --> 28:13.025
Let me be clear, sir.

28:13.275 --> 28:14.902
I intend to fulfill all my duties

28:14.985 --> 28:16.278
until the day I'm discharged.

28:17.070 --> 28:18.989
Enjoy your meal, sir. Salute.

28:33.295 --> 28:34.880
NAMPYO DISTRIBUTION

28:36.131 --> 28:38.467
HEALTHY KOREAN PORK

28:42.512 --> 28:45.140
SANMI DISTRIBUTION

28:49.311 --> 28:51.104
What exactly are these companies?

28:54.524 --> 29:01.657
SEONG-JAE'S TTEOKBOKKI

29:12.000 --> 29:14.544
To use your abilities
outside the Garrison Area

29:14.920 --> 29:17.256
you must be promoted to Advanced Cook.

29:33.272 --> 29:35.107
It tastes so much better now.
What's wrong?

29:35.190 --> 29:36.400
Remember?

29:36.483 --> 29:38.068
When you ate Dad's tteokbokki

29:38.902 --> 29:40.862
it had this subtle sweetness.

29:41.738 --> 29:43.573
I'm trying to find that subtle flavor

29:44.324 --> 29:45.784
but this just doesn't have it.

29:46.368 --> 29:47.744
- Oh, come on.
- Mrs. Kang!

29:47.869 --> 29:50.289
If it isn't our favorite customer.

29:50.372 --> 29:52.040
- I'm here!
- Hey.

29:53.917 --> 29:56.211
Kang Seong-jae, how could you?

29:56.920 --> 29:59.798
I have to hear you're on leave
from Eun-jae, huh?

30:00.841 --> 30:03.969
- Oh dear, my son was in the wrong.
- I know, right?

30:04.177 --> 30:05.846
This isn't it.

30:05.929 --> 30:07.723
So what, are you saying
you did nothing wrong?

30:08.598 --> 30:09.766
I'm sorry.

30:10.309 --> 30:11.977
I was just concentrating.

30:12.311 --> 30:13.312
You're here?

30:20.402 --> 30:23.196
Why do I even like a guy like him?

30:23.280 --> 30:24.614
Because he's handsome.

30:26.825 --> 30:29.995
I think the army turned him into
a kitchen god or something.

30:30.203 --> 30:31.955
Cooking in the army wasn't enough.

30:32.039 --> 30:33.332
He's still at it on his leave.

30:33.790 --> 30:34.958
Tell me about it.

30:36.084 --> 30:38.211
Okay, that's enough.

30:38.295 --> 30:39.755
Go eat something nice with Min-a.

30:39.838 --> 30:42.341
-But let me just finish this.
-Go on.

30:42.424 --> 30:43.467
I'll finish up here.

30:43.550 --> 30:45.135
- Thank you so much.
- Of course.

30:45.218 --> 30:47.012
- Let's go.
- Don't you come back here.

30:49.181 --> 30:50.182
Go.

30:52.267 --> 30:54.311
You're really something else,
doing this even on your leave.

30:55.228 --> 30:56.480
Isn't there anything you wanted to do?

30:58.982 --> 31:00.859
There was something I wanted to do.

31:04.696 --> 31:06.406
SKILL USE UNAVAILABLE
LEFT THE GARRISON AREA

31:06.490 --> 31:08.158
I didn't expect to be blocked like this.

31:09.284 --> 31:10.702
Want to go get something good to eat?

31:11.495 --> 31:13.372
There's a great whole chicken
soup place over there.

31:16.750 --> 31:19.628
INVINCIBLE BUNSIK
GHOST-CATCHING TTEOKBOKKI

31:29.763 --> 31:32.599
Hey, don't tell me you want
to eat tteokbokki again.

31:32.808 --> 31:34.643
The wait is at least two hours here.

31:35.143 --> 31:37.646
If it's worth spending that much
of our precious time...

31:38.105 --> 31:40.816
I'm curious just how good it must be.

31:44.736 --> 31:45.737
Let's go.

31:48.949 --> 31:53.495
GHOST-CATCHING TTEOKBOKKI

31:55.622 --> 31:57.958
Waiting number 320, trainee.

31:59.167 --> 32:00.419
- Yes?
- From now on

32:00.502 --> 32:03.547
you'll answer everything
with "Ak!" Understood?

32:05.298 --> 32:06.299
- Ak!
- Ak!

32:06.383 --> 32:07.384
Run.

32:07.759 --> 32:08.927
Go!

32:13.765 --> 32:16.393
IF ANYONE COULD MAKE DELICIOUS TTEOKBOKKI

32:16.476 --> 32:19.646
I NEVER WOULD HAVE CHOSEN TO SELL IT

32:30.449 --> 32:33.660
Usually, places like this
don't have good food.

32:50.010 --> 32:52.637
You will now enjoy your meal. Go!

32:53.638 --> 32:55.015
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat!

33:14.951 --> 33:17.829
This just looks like ordinary tteokbokki.

33:17.913 --> 33:19.873
How is the flavor so deep?

33:19.956 --> 33:22.000
It's spicy, with a subtle sweetness

33:22.083 --> 33:23.752
that balances it all out.

33:25.295 --> 33:26.588
This is so good!

33:26.671 --> 33:27.672
Yeah.

33:34.971 --> 33:35.972
Damn it.

33:42.312 --> 33:43.313
Salute!

33:44.022 --> 33:45.232
What are you doing here?

33:45.315 --> 33:47.067
I thought you only ate frozen meals.

33:47.150 --> 33:48.360
I'm here for kitchen duty, sir.

33:49.444 --> 33:51.363
Tell them we don't need any help.

33:52.948 --> 33:53.990
Surely...

33:54.574 --> 33:55.951
you don't need this either?

33:56.034 --> 33:57.827
RECIPE NOTEBOOK
KANG SEONG-JAE

33:59.538 --> 34:02.499
Kang Seong-jae thought
you might need this...

34:02.582 --> 34:03.667
so he left it with me.

34:04.834 --> 34:06.336
I'd forgotten about it, sir.

34:12.175 --> 34:13.510
RECIPE NOTEBOOK
KANG SEONG-JAE

34:16.346 --> 34:17.472
Why are you giving this to me?

34:17.556 --> 34:20.934
The timing doesn't seem right
for me to give it to him, sir.

34:21.017 --> 34:22.018
No way.

34:22.102 --> 34:23.270
I'm too scared to talk to him.

34:25.480 --> 34:27.107
I wrote down what I learned here

34:27.190 --> 34:29.276
in this notebook.

34:29.776 --> 34:31.653
So, if Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun

34:31.736 --> 34:33.196
looks through it whenever he needs to

34:33.572 --> 34:36.700
then when the other seniors eat here

34:36.783 --> 34:38.994
won't they enjoy
their meals a little more?

34:40.078 --> 34:42.831
Carefully wash the bean sprouts
and dry them.

34:42.914 --> 34:47.377
Carefully, stir-fry the broth,
anchovies, oil, and sauce...

34:47.836 --> 34:49.754
Carefully, carefully, carefully.

34:50.714 --> 34:54.676
This little punk is trying
to teach me now, is he?

34:54.759 --> 34:56.136
"Carefully"?

34:56.219 --> 34:57.762
Does being "careful"
put food on the table?

35:08.565 --> 35:11.568
WE ARE NOW CLOSED

35:17.866 --> 35:19.242
- Hello, sir.
- Who are you?

35:19.326 --> 35:21.161
I'm the one
who came for tteokbokki this afternoon.

35:22.245 --> 35:23.705
You ate this afternoon.

35:23.913 --> 35:24.914
Why are you here at this hour?

35:26.416 --> 35:28.543
I'm not here to cause any trouble.

35:31.796 --> 35:32.964
The tteokbokki...

35:33.173 --> 35:34.507
I would like to learn from you.

35:42.182 --> 35:44.934
Do I look like a pushover to you?

35:45.977 --> 35:48.313
So many tried to steal my recipe

35:48.396 --> 35:50.774
I could line them all up for 20 laps.

35:56.905 --> 35:58.365
My mother runs a food truck alone

35:58.448 --> 36:00.200
ever since my father passed away.

36:00.283 --> 36:01.576
But she's still struggling.

36:03.161 --> 36:04.579
I'm a New Recruit on my first leave

36:04.829 --> 36:06.373
and I have to return to my base soon.

36:07.999 --> 36:09.918
I'm desperate to learn how
before I go back.

36:17.634 --> 36:20.220
I'm not shamelessly begging you
to just tell me.

36:21.388 --> 36:22.806
I want to work alongside you

36:23.723 --> 36:27.185
and find my own way
to make delicious tteokbokki.

36:29.187 --> 36:30.397
If you'll help me...

36:32.273 --> 36:33.400
I'll do anything.

36:43.493 --> 36:46.788
You'll really do anything?

36:48.832 --> 36:50.834
Yes, I will do anything.

36:52.544 --> 36:54.212
I'll ask you one more time.

36:54.295 --> 36:56.673
Will you do anything?

37:00.719 --> 37:02.929
First, let's see how determined you are.

37:03.221 --> 37:05.390
Are you going to use all of this today?

37:05.724 --> 37:08.518
We're famous nationwide. This is nothing.

37:09.060 --> 37:11.354
I'm giving you exactly 30 minutes.
How many minutes?

37:12.605 --> 37:14.816
- 30 minutes.
- I can't hear you!

37:15.024 --> 37:17.402
- 20 minutes. 15 minutes.
- I misheard!

37:17.485 --> 37:20.488
We get it done! Marine Corps spirit!

37:50.101 --> 37:51.728
GHOST-CATCHING TTEOKBOKKI
ONCE A CUSTOMER, FOREVER A CUSTOMER

38:05.867 --> 38:08.953
The proper oil temperature is 180 degrees.

38:09.204 --> 38:11.498
Control the flame so it doesn't overheat.

38:15.960 --> 38:17.253
Have a good one.

38:18.213 --> 38:20.340
Here's your tteokbokki. Enjoy.

38:21.758 --> 38:23.468
Salute! Welcome.

38:23.551 --> 38:24.594
Right this way, please.

38:53.289 --> 38:54.833
Is he finally satisfied?

39:00.797 --> 39:03.132
I didn't mean to drag you into this.

39:04.509 --> 39:07.095
Well, I wasn't exactly planning
on doing charity work myself

39:07.470 --> 39:09.848
but I could tell by his face
he wasn't going to make it easy.

39:11.140 --> 39:14.894
When it comes to
pleasing bosses, I'm a pro.

39:16.104 --> 39:17.105
Sir.

39:17.605 --> 39:20.024
Did you cook my willpower
into this sauce or something?

39:20.733 --> 39:24.070
I'm supposed to be on a diet,
but I just can't stop.

39:26.573 --> 39:28.157
The owner said something.

39:29.033 --> 39:30.535
He said you talk too much.

39:31.828 --> 39:32.829
Whatever.

39:33.288 --> 39:34.664
So, did you figure it out?

39:35.582 --> 39:36.583
The secret, I mean.

39:39.878 --> 39:41.588
No, not yet.

39:42.255 --> 39:44.674
You have to go back soon.
You should take a break.

39:45.466 --> 39:47.760
You'll just wear yourself out.

39:47.844 --> 39:49.053
It's hard...

39:51.931 --> 39:52.932
But it's fun.

39:54.976 --> 39:57.645
I spend all day frying things
in front of hot oil

39:58.146 --> 39:59.939
and I watch them get more and more

40:00.023 --> 40:01.733
golden brown and delicious.

40:01.816 --> 40:02.942
As I kept doing it

40:03.276 --> 40:05.653
by the end,
I made the best fried food ever.

40:08.781 --> 40:11.326
I always knew you were weird

40:12.035 --> 40:14.037
but I think you've gotten even weirder.

40:16.706 --> 40:17.999
Me? I'm weird?

40:18.416 --> 40:19.417
Yep.

40:19.959 --> 40:20.960
Don't you remember?

40:38.227 --> 40:39.270
What, over there?

40:39.354 --> 40:41.064
It looks like a UFO is invading Earth.

40:42.440 --> 40:44.025
Oh, no, it's just...

40:46.653 --> 40:48.947
I imagined the field
just splitting in half...

40:49.322 --> 40:50.323
and cracking right open.

40:50.740 --> 40:53.868
Then I imagined a giant dragon
that had slept for ages waking up.

40:53.952 --> 40:56.037
And the dragon started rampaging
through the buildings.

41:08.257 --> 41:10.385
Hey, when it comes to being weird

41:10.468 --> 41:12.011
you always had to one-up me.

41:12.095 --> 41:14.389
Hey, honestly, I wasn't that bad.

41:14.847 --> 41:17.350
I was just hamming it up
to become your friend.

41:18.184 --> 41:20.895
Must have been so tough,
having to go along with my nonsense.

41:21.938 --> 41:23.147
But that's what made it fun.

41:23.231 --> 41:24.440
Being with you.

41:25.066 --> 41:27.527
Even if we were just talking about
silly, nonsensical things

41:27.735 --> 41:29.654
we'd laugh so hard
we'd lose all track of time.

41:46.421 --> 41:47.463
Okay, what if...

41:51.384 --> 41:52.927
you suddenly got a special ability?

41:54.053 --> 41:55.138
And all of a sudden

41:55.221 --> 41:58.016
you start hearing a strange voice.

41:58.099 --> 41:59.225
Welcome.

41:59.726 --> 42:00.810
Hero.

42:00.893 --> 42:02.603
Private Kang Seong-jae.

42:02.979 --> 42:04.439
It tells you to start leveling up.

42:05.898 --> 42:09.152
Level up and grow stronger.

42:09.235 --> 42:11.821
All you do gives Experience Points

42:11.904 --> 42:13.781
and you can even learn skills.

42:13.865 --> 42:14.907
And on top of that

42:14.991 --> 42:16.993
there are daily quests to complete.

42:17.076 --> 42:18.077
So...

42:19.996 --> 42:22.040
What's the first thing you'd want to do?

42:25.376 --> 42:26.627
That sounds a lot like
my situation right now.

42:27.920 --> 42:29.422
I'm an intern on contract

42:29.505 --> 42:31.632
and I always hear my supervisors.

42:32.300 --> 42:33.718
They say, "Everything you do now"

42:33.801 --> 42:36.262
"is valuable experience, so try hard."

42:36.637 --> 42:39.474
If I were you, I'd take the chance
to rack up all the Experience Points.

42:39.724 --> 42:41.017
If I level up enough, who knows?

42:41.100 --> 42:42.310
I might get hired full-time.

42:48.941 --> 42:52.195
Do you think I could become
a better person than I am now?

42:55.156 --> 42:57.241
You're already a great person as you are.

42:58.451 --> 42:59.660
Everyone knows it except you.

43:25.394 --> 43:26.395
All right!

43:44.122 --> 43:46.582
Master Sergeant said have Kang Seong-jae
do this when he gets back...

43:47.667 --> 43:48.668
Dedication?

43:49.460 --> 43:51.254
I'll show you
what real dedication looks like.

44:08.563 --> 44:09.605
Salute!

44:10.648 --> 44:13.317
Whoa, why is it so hazy in here?

44:13.693 --> 44:14.986
Someone open a window.

44:15.987 --> 44:16.988
What the...?

44:17.905 --> 44:18.906
Goodness gracious!

44:21.367 --> 44:22.368
What is this?

44:25.913 --> 44:26.914
Hey now

44:26.998 --> 44:28.166
is this what's on the menu today?

44:29.917 --> 44:32.295
I got tired of waiting for
Kang Seong-jae, sir.

44:32.378 --> 44:33.379
You punk!

44:33.462 --> 44:35.047
You think you can just
mess with this precious meal?

44:35.131 --> 44:36.549
Letting you handle it?

44:36.632 --> 44:38.801
Good grief, this is driving me nuts.

44:38.885 --> 44:40.678
Yoon Dong-hyun,
how many times have I told you?

44:41.012 --> 44:42.388
Cooking is a delicate art.

44:42.471 --> 44:44.849
The cook's touch is everything.

44:44.932 --> 44:47.268
- Someone all thumbs like you...
- Dedication!

44:55.026 --> 44:56.068
Dedication, what?

45:01.073 --> 45:02.658
If I told you every time the yellow fat
surfaced

45:02.742 --> 45:04.744
I skimmed it, and skimmed it
again and again

45:04.827 --> 45:06.746
and that I boiled this
for 20 hours straight...

45:07.830 --> 45:09.207
would you believe me, sir?

45:13.336 --> 45:14.587
Still, the broth looks like

45:14.670 --> 45:16.422
it was rendered quite well, sir.

45:17.131 --> 45:18.466
What, you don't know how he operates?

45:19.300 --> 45:20.927
He's the type to dump coffee creamer

45:21.010 --> 45:22.678
in there just to make it look right.

45:23.554 --> 45:24.555
Jeez.

45:32.480 --> 45:33.481
What is this?

45:36.776 --> 45:37.944
Wait a second.

46:42.049 --> 46:43.259
Jae-young...

46:44.719 --> 46:46.387
No. Don't come here.

46:48.931 --> 46:50.266
Stay away!

47:34.352 --> 47:35.394
No!

48:25.152 --> 48:26.153
What was that?

48:30.241 --> 48:31.242
Is this it?

48:31.909 --> 48:34.703
I did my best, sir.

48:34.787 --> 48:35.788
Wait...

48:38.332 --> 48:39.500
Can I go home now?

48:39.583 --> 48:41.585
What is this? It feels unfinished.

48:41.669 --> 48:42.837
When are you gonna pay me?

48:44.296 --> 48:45.631
It's strange.

48:46.173 --> 48:48.426
It has the makings of a rich broth

48:48.676 --> 48:50.803
but it's also not.

48:50.886 --> 48:52.513
It's a very peculiar taste.

48:52.596 --> 48:54.723
It really is, sir. It's so...

48:55.683 --> 48:57.059
Well, at least it's edible.
That's something.

48:57.143 --> 48:58.936
I still feel a little iffy about it.

48:59.562 --> 49:00.938
But still, if this is the result

49:01.147 --> 49:02.648
I guess he's finally
shaping up before discharge.

49:03.399 --> 49:05.317
See? Didn't I tell you I could do it, sir?

49:06.986 --> 49:07.987
What did you say?

49:08.946 --> 49:11.824
I said I could do it, didn't I?

49:13.534 --> 49:15.161
He makes a fuss even when
I compliment him.

49:26.005 --> 49:27.256
- Please, have a seat.
- Okay.

49:34.263 --> 49:35.264
Thank you.

49:41.395 --> 49:43.481
I've learned so much thanks to you, sir.

49:43.689 --> 49:44.690
Thank you.

49:46.692 --> 49:48.360
You return to base tomorrow, right?

49:49.653 --> 49:50.654
Yes.

49:51.071 --> 49:52.573
I thought seven days and six nights

49:52.656 --> 49:54.575
would feel like a long time...

49:55.242 --> 49:57.703
but it went by in the blink of an eye.

49:58.370 --> 49:59.371
So...

49:59.497 --> 50:01.790
did you find the answer
you were looking for?

50:04.835 --> 50:05.836
No.

50:06.128 --> 50:07.171
But...

50:07.546 --> 50:08.714
I feel like I've gotten

50:08.797 --> 50:10.132
the hang of deep-frying.

50:10.424 --> 50:11.425
It was fun.

50:12.510 --> 50:13.969
Next time you're on leave

50:14.053 --> 50:16.972
just come by with your girlfriend.

50:17.431 --> 50:19.850
Even if we're full,
I'll make a spot for you.

50:30.277 --> 50:32.404
Oh, no, sir. I couldn't.

50:32.488 --> 50:36.659
Please, take it. It's the least I can do.

50:44.833 --> 50:45.834
Thank you.

50:52.091 --> 50:54.468
Gosh, where did these
ripe persimmons come from?

50:54.552 --> 50:56.720
The owner gave them to me
for my hard work.

50:59.056 --> 51:01.559
You worked your whole leave
without any rest.

51:01.976 --> 51:03.102
I feel so bad.

51:03.644 --> 51:05.437
Mom, what is there to feel bad about?

51:05.521 --> 51:06.605
I wanted to do it.

51:07.106 --> 51:08.315
But, still.

51:09.692 --> 51:11.277
My goodness.

51:11.860 --> 51:13.487
I'm so thankful for him.

51:15.114 --> 51:16.115
Should we try one?

51:19.243 --> 51:21.704
- Oh, you have it, son.
- No, you have it first, Mom.

51:21.787 --> 51:24.248
Really? Wow, it's huge.

51:28.961 --> 51:30.921
- This is delicious.
- It is.

51:32.590 --> 51:34.925
It's spicy, with a subtle sweetness

51:35.009 --> 51:36.677
that balances it all out.

51:41.390 --> 51:42.391
So this is the secret.

52:50.876 --> 52:52.419
The sweet persimmon flavor

52:52.503 --> 52:54.213
is so uplifting.

52:55.339 --> 52:57.925
I thought the spicier
the tteokbokki, the better

52:58.759 --> 53:01.470
but this just shattered
my whole worldview on tteokbokki.

53:09.645 --> 53:12.398
Our tteokbokki's getting
rave reviews from customers.

53:12.648 --> 53:14.274
I'll hold down the fort here.

53:14.358 --> 53:15.818
Yes. Enjoy your meal.

53:16.902 --> 53:18.195
Oh, by the way,

53:18.487 --> 53:21.323
I feel terrible that
I couldn't even see you off.

53:21.407 --> 53:23.367
Don't be. You are busy.

53:24.410 --> 53:25.786
I'll have another leave again soon.

53:27.371 --> 53:28.372
Yeah.

53:28.747 --> 53:31.375
I'll keep practicing my cooking here.

53:31.625 --> 53:32.626
Son

53:32.710 --> 53:34.211
don't worry about us at home, okay?

53:34.461 --> 53:36.839
Always take care
of your health, all right?

53:37.172 --> 53:38.757
And give Min-a a call.

53:39.049 --> 53:40.342
You don't want her to feel left out.

53:42.469 --> 53:43.470
Okay.

53:44.179 --> 53:45.431
I'll call you again once I'm back on base.

53:55.524 --> 53:57.735
Welcome back to the Garrison Area.

53:58.736 --> 54:01.238
Skill usage restriction has been lifted.

54:02.906 --> 54:04.658
I'm going to give it my all

54:06.493 --> 54:07.870
so I'm counting on you.

54:22.384 --> 54:23.719
Salute!

54:24.970 --> 54:26.096
Salute.

54:27.639 --> 54:29.641
Private Kang Seong-jae.

54:29.850 --> 54:32.853
Reporting my return from leave
as of 18:00 hours today!

54:32.936 --> 54:34.146
Salute!

54:35.647 --> 54:36.690
Salute.

54:37.858 --> 54:39.067
Did you have a good leave?

54:39.943 --> 54:42.196
Yes, ma'am. I learned a great deal
while I was out.

54:44.031 --> 54:46.867
But I bet seeing your family
was a relief, right?

54:47.159 --> 54:49.787
Yes, ma'am. It made me determined
to work even harder.

54:50.204 --> 54:52.831
I'll ensure the outpost soldiers
get three satisfying meals a day.

54:54.124 --> 54:55.667
Good. Keep up the hard work.

54:56.043 --> 54:58.045
But you're in for a rough time
now that you're back.

54:59.963 --> 55:01.256
I'm sorry?

55:01.548 --> 55:02.966
PARK JAE-YOUNG

55:04.176 --> 55:05.636
What rotten luck.

55:06.678 --> 55:09.848
Of all the rotten luck,
it had to clash with your vacation.

55:09.932 --> 55:12.392
NOTICE: ALL LEAVE SUSPENDED
FOR KCTC TRAINING

55:12.476 --> 55:14.102
29TH DIVISION ANNOUNCEMENT

55:16.438 --> 55:18.398
I'm just... speechless.

55:22.861 --> 55:24.571
Hey, pull yourself together. Okay?

55:25.030 --> 55:26.323
This is nothing.

55:28.450 --> 55:30.285
It's nothing, I tell you. Okay?

55:31.662 --> 55:33.622
Oh, you poor guy.

55:33.705 --> 55:35.624
You poor, poor guy.

55:36.583 --> 55:40.087
Dong-hyeon, even if you try
to stop the clock

55:40.462 --> 55:41.922
your military service will end.

55:42.005 --> 55:44.967
You hear me? It will.

55:45.968 --> 55:47.219
Calm down.

55:49.012 --> 55:50.722
KCTC...

55:51.390 --> 55:52.724
Why!

55:59.273 --> 56:00.816
An army marches on its stomach.

56:01.233 --> 56:02.734
Boost your unit's morale

56:02.818 --> 56:05.320
and lead them to victory in the KCTC.

56:05.946 --> 56:07.322
Upon completing the Quest

56:07.406 --> 56:10.659
you'll earn double
Experience Points for one week.

56:12.202 --> 56:13.203
Double?

56:29.553 --> 56:31.513
We've located the platoon commander.

56:32.681 --> 56:33.724
Move to that position.

57:03.503 --> 57:05.380
Enemy platoon eliminated.

57:19.853 --> 57:21.480
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTORS RA MI-RAN, JIN
GOO, PARK MYUNG-HOON, AND SEO JEONG-YEON

57:43.210 --> 57:45.629
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

57:46.380 --> 57:48.465
This is on a whole other level.

57:49.383 --> 57:51.760
You did say we had to protect
the kitchen trailer, sir.

57:52.803 --> 57:53.804
We're going to get bombed!

57:53.887 --> 57:55.973
We're all going to die if this keeps up.

57:56.848 --> 57:58.016
Battalion Commander!

57:58.684 --> 58:00.268
Our supply route has been cut off.

58:00.352 --> 58:02.020
Morale is falling.

58:02.104 --> 58:03.730
Can't you see I'm dying here
because of you?

58:04.147 --> 58:05.607
Do you know the supply vehicle's location?

58:05.857 --> 58:07.275
If it's not far away...

58:07.359 --> 58:08.527
I'll infiltrate.

58:08.652 --> 58:10.320
Once a soldier draws his weapon...

58:10.696 --> 58:12.614
- Bring it on!
- He has to finish the fight, right?

58:12.698 --> 58:14.783
I suddenly feel full of energy.

58:16.785 --> 58:17.786
Hands up!
